==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hundrað|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hundaradą}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*hundą}} (< {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*ḱm̥tóm}}) + {{m|gem-pro|*radą||count}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhʏntraːð/|lang=is}}

===Numeral===
{{is-noun|n}}

# '''[[hundred]]''' (100); the cardinal number after [[níutíu og níu#Icelandic|níutíu og níu]] and before [[hundrað og einn#Icelandic|hundrað og einn]].
#* Genesis 5:3 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Fyrsta%20bók%20Móse+5:3&version=ICELAND Icelandic], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Fyrsta%20b%C3%B3k%20M%C3%B3se%205:3&version=NIV English])
#*: ''Adam lifði '''hundrað''' og þrjátíu ár. Þá gat hann son í líking sinni, eftir sinni mynd, og nefndi hann Set.''
#*:: When Adam had lived '''1'''30 years, he had a son in his own likeness, in his own image; and he named him Seth.

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-n-s|h|u|ndr|a|ð}}
The irregular genitive plural ''hundruða'', ''hundruðanna'' also exists.

